Id: pass019w
Severity: WARN
Category: accounts
Check: check_passwdspec
Fix: Set PASS_MAX_DAYS and PASS_WARN_AGE in login.defs; chage -M for existing accounts.
References: login.defs(5); chage(1)
Controls: CIS 5.2; NIST IA-5(1); ISO 5.17; CE User access control

The account has no password aging: the password never expires and
there is no warning before it would. Set PASS_MAX_DAYS and PASS_WARN_AGE
in /etc/login.defs for new accounts and use chage for existing ones,
unless your policy is deliberately to rely on length and no rotation.
